y but  we use a center third rail to get all  our traction and braking a typical  railway  they get all their traction and braking  through the outside rails  instead there's a center rail the cog  underneath the train hooks into  basically pulls the train up the  mountain  a groundbreaking system when it was  constructed in 1891  as saloons dominated the local landscape  against the backdrop of gold rush  fortunes  with the broadport and the cog railway  you really get a sense of what the old  wild west used to be like  absolutely we believe that the broadmoor  is kind of the  gateway to the american west the nearby  broadmoor hotel  owns the railway today president and ceo  jack demoli how did the idea for this  even come about  well there was a gentleman that was  staying at a motel in manitou springs  by the name of mr simmons he might have  made a mattress or two  beautyrest by simmons the do not disturb  mattress  yes that simmons zalman simmons was  also the inventor of the beautyrest  mattress his inspiration  a tedious two-day mule ride to the  summit  for a telegraph line inspection  passengers climbed aboard just  two years of construction later was it  innovative for its time  without a doubt and you think about 1891  and the fact that not too many railroads  were running in the united states period  let alone up america's mountain  as the years passed the trains  technology evolved with 20th century  innovation  the locomotives actually started with  wood fired  then went from wood fire to to steam  powered  and then from steam powered to  diesel-powered  in all the world there are only three  similar roads  but much of the railway's infrastructure  remained in place for more than 125  years  that was until 2018 when it shut down  for renovations  totaling more than a hundred million  dollars we looked at everything when we  did this project the track  the trains the depot facility that we're  at right now  and we retrofitted some of our older  equipmen